00:03:48.916 --> 00:03:51.801
- Fact number four, he did
a cameo roll as himself

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:55.110
in the film Shallow Hal
starring Jack Black.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.787
- Hey, it's you.

00:03:56.787 --> 00:03:58.505
You're the TV guru guy.

00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:00.394
- Yes, Tony Robbins, please to meet you.

00:04:00.394 --> 00:04:01.573
- Yeah.

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:03.957
- Well, it was interesting the
Farley brothers are friends

00:04:03.957 --> 00:04:07.087
and fans and they're
brilliant, funny, crazy guys.

00:04:07.087 --> 00:04:08.691
And they invited me to
participate in the movie

00:04:08.691 --> 00:04:10.905
and I didn't turn them
down, I just said no

00:04:10.905 --> 00:04:13.080
because it just wasn't for me.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.653
And when they brought me
the script I was moved

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:17.266
by it because the message
is about inner-beauty

00:04:17.266 --> 00:04:19.225
and not being a surface-driven person,

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.013
which is part of what my life's about.

00:04:21.013 --> 00:04:23.571
Hypothetical situation,
which do you prefer,

00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:27.413
a girlfriend missing one
breast or half a brain?

00:04:27.413 --> 00:04:29.281
- Ew, toughie.

00:04:29.281 --> 00:04:31.090
- And then I found out that the story

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.564
was written by a man who'd bought

00:04:32.564 --> 00:04:35.267
my personal power audio
program off of television,

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:36.617
off an infomercial years ago.

00:04:36.617 --> 00:04:37.705
So, I said, yeah, I want to do this.

00:04:37.705 --> 00:04:39.473
And I wasn't originally in the script.

00:04:39.473 --> 00:04:41.708
They were using this, like,
seance guy to do this.

00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:42.852
You've got a pattern of looking at women

00:04:42.852 --> 00:04:44.398
and judging them by the exterior.

00:04:44.398 --> 00:04:45.942
You know, they wrote the script

00:04:45.942 --> 00:04:47.539
and none of it was really me and I said,

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:48.624
you know, I've memorized this

00:04:48.624 --> 00:04:49.984
and I'm very respectful,
you put me in the middle

00:04:49.984 --> 00:04:52.464
of this movie as a central character,

00:04:52.464 --> 00:04:54.020
but this is not what I'd say.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.943
So, I'll do what you want,

00:04:54.943 --> 00:04:57.157
but can I just show you what I really do?

00:04:57.157 --> 00:04:58.406
And they go, Tony, it's a movie.

00:04:58.406 --> 00:04:59.995
I said just let me try.

00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:01.352
- Can you think of one specific time when

00:05:01.352 --> 00:05:04.176
you were really shallow?
- Oh yeah, I got one.

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:05.597
- Think about that, ready?
- I got a good one.

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:07.097
- Devils come out.

00:05:07.998 --> 00:05:09.801
- What the hell are you
doing, banana hands?

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.621
- So, that heeled scene when
I smack him on the head,

00:05:11.621 --> 00:05:13.235
he had no idea that was coming.

00:05:13.235 --> 00:05:14.472
They had no idea it was coming.

00:05:14.472 --> 00:05:16.050
In fact, they laughed
so hard when it happened

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.569
that his reactions are not fake reactions,

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:19.504
they're actual reactions.

00:05:19.504 --> 00:05:20.560
They were real reactions 'cause

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.515
he didn't know it was coming.

00:05:21.515 --> 00:05:23.231
And then they shot the thing 15 angles

00:05:23.231 --> 00:05:24.247
'cause everybody was laughing so hard

00:05:24.247 --> 00:05:25.913
cameras were shaking and everything else.

00:05:25.913 --> 00:05:27.062
But that's my approach.

00:05:27.062 --> 00:05:30.088
My approach is jar people
into reality quickly,

00:05:30.088 --> 00:05:31.378
not talk about things.

00:05:31.378 --> 00:05:33.297
It was a great privilege
to be part of the film

00:05:33.297 --> 00:05:35.848
and I have no desire to be an actor,

00:05:35.848 --> 00:05:38.962
but I'm grateful that I was
part of that great little story.

00:05:38.962 --> 00:05:42.056
- Fact number five, U.S.
President Bill Clinton

00:05:42.056 --> 00:05:44.584
called him before he was impeached.

00:05:44.584 --> 00:05:47.083
- I get a phone call
where a child is suicidal

00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:48.565
or the President of
the United States calls

00:05:48.565 --> 00:05:49.847
and says they're going to
impeach me in the morning.

00:05:49.847 --> 00:05:50.680
What should I do?

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.928
- So that actually happened?
- That actually happened.

00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:53.730
- Bill Clinton called you the night before

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.552
in 1998 and said Tony,
they may be impeaching me

00:05:56.552 --> 00:05:57.944
in the morning, what should I do.

00:05:57.944 --> 00:06:00.047
What an extraordinary position

00:06:00.047 --> 00:06:01.520
of responsibility that you have.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.729
- Well, I'm sure I'm not
the only person he called.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:03.572
(laughing)

00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:04.690
- You're one of the people he called.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.732
- By any stretch and yes.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:07.932
- Just step back for a moment.

00:06:07.932 --> 00:06:09.862
That moment, how did you feel?

00:06:09.862 --> 00:06:12.198
Despite all these incredible
things you've experienced,

00:06:12.198 --> 00:06:14.425
to have the President of your country

00:06:14.425 --> 00:06:18.150
call you in his great hour of need.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.684
- If you're thinking about yourself

00:06:19.684 --> 00:06:21.272
in a moment like that
you can't really serve.

00:06:21.272 --> 00:06:23.051
So, then it'd be all about you.

00:06:23.051 --> 00:06:24.705
What I felt was a sense of responsibility

00:06:24.705 --> 00:06:26.798
and I also felt I need
to sell him straight

00:06:26.798 --> 00:06:27.846
of what I really believed.

00:06:27.846 --> 00:06:29.674
And I knew he was going
to get different opinions

00:06:29.674 --> 00:06:30.638
and I don't really talk about what

00:06:30.638 --> 00:06:32.141
I do with someone unless
they speak about it,

00:06:32.141 --> 00:06:33.868
but I did speak at that point

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:35.179
and said, frankly, you
know, you're not going to

00:06:35.179 --> 00:06:36.643
be impeached in the
morning, easy for me to say,

00:06:36.643 --> 00:06:37.830
I'm not in your position.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.163
It's just politically
it's not going to happen.

00:06:39.163 --> 00:06:41.133
But what you have to decide is
what's your legacy going to be.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:42.291
What's your outcome?

00:06:42.291 --> 00:06:44.425
Because you have to decide what
you're going to be able to say

00:06:44.425 --> 00:06:46.294
that people at home can
tell their children about.

00:06:46.294 --> 00:06:47.806
You have to look at
what you can do legally.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:49.667
But if I were you I'd be
doing what you know is right

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.127
and nothing less than that process.

00:06:51.127 --> 00:06:53.934
'Cause you want to be able
to look yourself in the face.

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.750
- Fact number six, the best advice

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.553
he ever got was also from Jim Rohn.

00:06:58.553 --> 00:07:00.949
- What's the best piece of
advice you've ever gotten?

00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:02.733
- God, that's so much, but I think one of

00:07:02.733 --> 00:07:04.840
the most important ones
was early in my life

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.995
one of my mentors named Jim Rohn said,

00:07:06.995 --> 00:07:08.825
"Tony, all you have to focus on your life

00:07:08.825 --> 00:07:11.542
is find a way to add more
value than anybody else does

00:07:11.542 --> 00:07:13.309
and you'll never have
to worry about anything.

00:07:13.309 --> 00:07:15.475
Be the person that does more for others

00:07:15.475 --> 00:07:18.055
and life will just be
anything you want out of it,"

00:07:18.055 --> 00:07:18.969
really is what it is, so.

00:07:18.969 --> 00:07:20.432
And he also said the way to do that

00:07:20.432 --> 00:07:22.544
is every day work harder on
yourself than anything else.

00:07:22.544 --> 00:07:25.035
'Cause if you become more
intelligent, more valuable,

00:07:25.035 --> 00:07:28.317
more skilled you can add
more value to other people.

00:07:28.317 --> 00:07:30.276
- Fact number seven, he wants to feed

00:07:30.276 --> 00:07:33.194
over one billion people over Thanksgiving.

00:07:33.194 --> 00:07:36.005
- You were growing up, you
were really poor, right?

00:07:36.005 --> 00:07:37.164
- Extremely.
- Extremely poor.

00:07:37.164 --> 00:07:39.106
- We had no money for
Thanksgiving for food.

00:07:39.106 --> 00:07:43.199
It's part of why last year I
started feeding when I was 17.

00:07:43.199 --> 00:07:45.808
I started feeding families
since I was fed when I was 11.

00:07:45.808 --> 00:07:49.111
And I fed two families,
literally, and it was so moving,

00:07:49.111 --> 00:07:50.502
I said I'm going to
double it, I went to four

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:52.382
and then to eight and
then it was, like, a game

00:07:52.382 --> 00:07:54.150
to see could I reach more people.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.335
And then I started with some of employees

00:07:56.335 --> 00:07:58.152
and then eventually got to
a million people a year,

00:07:58.152 --> 00:07:59.749
then two million and
then I started matching

00:07:59.749 --> 00:08:01.322
my foundation with two million.

00:08:01.322 --> 00:08:04.218
So, for 12 years I fed
four million people a year.

00:08:04.218 --> 00:08:05.853
And then when I was writing this book

00:08:05.853 --> 00:08:07.043
I'm interviewing, if you can imagine,

00:08:07.043 --> 00:08:08.323
all these people started with nothing

00:08:08.323 --> 00:08:09.481
and are multi-billionaires.

00:08:09.481 --> 00:08:11.582
At the same time,
congress cut food stamps,

00:08:11.582 --> 00:08:14.316
called SNAP now, but it
was food stamps originally,

00:08:14.316 --> 00:08:16.143
by eight billion dollars.

00:08:16.143 --> 00:08:17.718
So, it's the equivalent,
to give ya an idea,

00:08:17.718 --> 00:08:20.328
of every family that's being supported

00:08:20.328 --> 00:08:22.159
giving up all their meals one week

00:08:22.159 --> 00:08:23.764
out of every month for 12 months.

00:08:23.764 --> 00:08:24.597
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:08:24.597 --> 00:08:26.222
- So, I decided I wanted
to do something about it,

00:08:26.222 --> 00:08:28.161
so I got a five million
dollar advance for the book.

00:08:28.161 --> 00:08:29.737
I gave all the money to Feeding America

00:08:29.737 --> 00:08:32.033
and then I said if I want
to feed 100 million people

00:08:32.033 --> 00:08:34.114
what do I got to do, so I
wrote a much bigger check

00:08:34.114 --> 00:08:36.847
and now I'm so, we did 102
million people last year,

00:08:36.847 --> 00:08:38.665
but now I'm going to do
100 million again this year

00:08:38.665 --> 00:08:40.067
and I got a plan to feed a billion people

00:08:40.067 --> 00:08:42.821
over the next ten years, so.

00:08:42.821 --> 00:08:44.984
It's so full circle from where I began.

00:08:44.984 --> 00:08:47.596
It's crazy and it's an
incredible privilege

00:08:47.596 --> 00:08:50.023
to be able to make a difference like that.

00:08:50.023 --> 00:08:52.635
- Fact number eight, he uses Cryotherapy

00:08:52.635 --> 00:08:55.904
to help his body recover
from being on stage all day.

00:08:55.904 --> 00:08:59.962
- I'm like an athlete, you got
to train your nervous system.

00:08:59.962 --> 00:09:01.572
Besides physically working out,

00:09:01.572 --> 00:09:03.586
I also train my mind to do and

00:09:03.586 --> 00:09:06.227
my emotions to do what's most difficult

00:09:06.227 --> 00:09:07.394
and I do that in all kinds of ways.

00:09:07.394 --> 00:09:08.732
I like to play at my edge.

00:09:08.732 --> 00:09:10.035
You know, that's how you get better.

00:09:10.035 --> 00:09:11.284
So, I put high demands on myself.

00:09:11.284 --> 00:09:12.453
But the first thing I do
every morning as part of

00:09:12.453 --> 00:09:14.973
that ritual is I jump in
a jacuzzi which loosens

00:09:14.973 --> 00:09:17.341
the muscles and then I jump
in freezing cold water.

00:09:17.341 --> 00:09:19.035
I have a cold plunge, if you would.

00:09:19.035 --> 00:09:21.921
It's 57 degrees and I
drop into that thing.

00:09:21.921 --> 00:09:24.704
I also for recover
sake, I use Cryotherapy,

00:09:24.704 --> 00:09:25.752
which was developed in Europe.

00:09:25.752 --> 00:09:26.757
It's amazing.

00:09:26.757 --> 00:09:28.516
A lot of athletes around
the world are using it now.

00:09:28.516 --> 00:09:31.917
And it lowers your body
temperature using nitrogens.

00:09:31.917 --> 00:09:34.132
So, there's no water on
you or you would freeze

00:09:34.132 --> 00:09:35.553
to death or you would burn.

00:09:35.553 --> 00:09:37.821
By using these gases it
brings the temperature down

00:09:37.821 --> 00:09:40.991
in your body down to minus 225 fahrenheit,

00:09:40.991 --> 00:09:43.408
which is my, well, for three minutes.

00:09:43.408 --> 00:09:46.293
And what it does is it like
resets your whole nervous system

00:09:46.293 --> 00:09:48.435
and it takes all the
inflammation out of your body.

00:09:48.435 --> 00:09:51.454
So, I'm on stage and I'll do 27 miles

00:09:51.454 --> 00:09:53.912
on my most intense day
of a three day program,

00:09:53.912 --> 00:09:56.499
so I'm doing, like, multiple
days of Ultramarathon.

00:09:56.499 --> 00:09:58.350
'Cause I'm not standing there talking.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.402
I mean, people would not come,

00:10:00.402 --> 00:10:01.947
people won't sit for a three hour movie

00:10:01.947 --> 00:10:04.829
someone spend 300 million
dollars on to make for two hours.

00:10:04.829 --> 00:10:07.107
If they're going to stay with
me for 50 hours over a weekend,

00:10:07.107 --> 00:10:08.500
I got to deliver, right?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.851
And I got the Paul Tudor Jones

00:10:09.851 --> 00:10:11.616
of the world in there, the Oprah Winfeys.

00:10:11.616 --> 00:10:13.527
Oprah tells me Tony I love ya,

00:10:13.527 --> 00:10:15.121
but I can't sit anywhere
for more than two hours

00:10:15.121 --> 00:10:16.313
and at the end of 12 hours she's standing

00:10:16.313 --> 00:10:17.471
in her chair going on camera

00:10:17.471 --> 00:10:19.280
"this is one of the greatest
experiences of my life".

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.291
Well, to do that, you
aren't standing still.

00:10:21.291 --> 00:10:22.834
I'm plunging the audience,
I'm doing things.

00:10:22.834 --> 00:10:26.135
I'm spontaneous, so that's a lot of miles.

00:10:26.135 --> 00:10:27.719
So, I'm literally doing one marathon

00:10:27.719 --> 00:10:30.048
and I go into this machine
and three minutes later

00:10:30.048 --> 00:10:31.590
I come out and the next day it's like

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.482
instead of all these
aches and pains and tears

00:10:33.482 --> 00:10:35.034
I'm recovered, so.

00:10:35.034 --> 00:10:36.487
I'm always looking for technology

00:10:36.487 --> 00:10:38.854
that can enhance my ability to perform

00:10:38.854 --> 00:10:42.977
and produce greater results
and also stay healthy.

00:10:42.977 --> 00:10:45.022
- And fact number nine,
he has one of the three

00:10:45.022 --> 00:10:48.220
most popular TED Talk videos of all time

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.220
for his talk "Why We Do What We Do".

00:10:52.072 --> 00:10:53.352
- Thank you.

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:55.799
I have to tell you I'm both
challenged and excited.

00:10:55.799 --> 00:10:58.499
My excitement is I get a
chance to give something back.

00:10:58.499 --> 00:11:00.309
My challenge is the shortest seminar

00:11:00.309 --> 00:11:03.580
I usually do is 50 hours.
(laughing)

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.034
I'm not exaggerating, I
do weekends and what I do,

00:11:06.034 --> 00:11:07.633
I do even more than that
obviously, coach people,

00:11:07.633 --> 00:11:10.855
but into emersion because
how'd you learn language?

00:11:10.855 --> 00:11:12.428
You didn't learn it by
just learning principals.

00:11:12.428 --> 00:11:15.162
You got in it and you did it
so often that it became real.

00:11:15.162 --> 00:11:17.040
And the bottom line of why I'm here,

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.402
besides being crazy mo-fo is that

00:11:19.402 --> 00:11:21.122
I'm really in a position, I'm not here

00:11:21.122 --> 00:11:22.943
to motivate you obviously,
you don't need that.

00:11:22.943 --> 00:11:24.642
A lot of times that's
what people think I do

00:11:24.642 --> 00:11:26.235
and it's the furthest thing from it.

00:11:26.235 --> 00:11:28.265
What happens though is people say to me

00:11:28.265 --> 00:11:29.630
"well, I don't need any
motivation" and I say

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.784
well, that's interesting,
that's not what I do.

00:11:31.784 --> 00:11:33.694
I'm the why guy.

00:11:33.694 --> 00:11:35.726
I want to know why you do what you do.

00:11:35.726 --> 00:11:38.333
What is your motive for action?

00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:40.286
What is it that drives
you in your life today,

00:11:40.286 --> 00:11:42.756
not ten years ago, are you
running the same pattern?

00:11:42.756 --> 00:11:44.828
Because I believe that the invisible force

00:11:44.828 --> 00:11:47.884
of internal drive activated is

00:11:47.884 --> 00:11:48.941
the most important thing in the world.

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:52.366
I'm here because I believe
emotion is the force of life.

00:11:52.366 --> 00:11:54.305
All of us here have great minds.

00:11:54.305 --> 00:11:56.377
You know, most of us
here have great minds.

00:11:56.377 --> 00:11:57.242
Right?
(laughing)

00:11:57.242 --> 00:11:58.075
I don't know if I'm in that category,

00:11:58.075 --> 00:11:59.607
but we all know how to
think and with our minds

00:11:59.607 --> 00:12:02.371
we can rationalize anything,
we can make anything happen.

00:12:02.371 --> 00:12:05.366
We can, I agree with what
was described a few days ago

00:12:05.366 --> 00:12:07.531
about this idea that people
work in their self-interest,

00:12:07.531 --> 00:12:10.556
but we all know that
that's bullshit at times.

00:12:10.556 --> 00:12:12.834
You don't work in your
self-interest all the time.

00:12:12.834 --> 00:12:14.430
Because when emotion comes into it

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.950
the wiring changes in
the way it functions.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:19.017
And so it's wonderful for
us to think intellectually

00:12:19.017 --> 00:12:20.650
about how the life of the world is

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:22.528
and especially those who are very smart.

00:12:22.528 --> 00:12:23.736
We can play this game in our head,

00:12:23.736 --> 00:12:25.567
but I really want to
know what's driving you

00:12:25.567 --> 00:12:27.293
and what I'd like to
maybe invite you to do

00:12:27.293 --> 00:12:29.029
by the end of this talk is explore

00:12:29.029 --> 00:12:31.052
where you are today, for two reasons.

00:12:31.052 --> 00:12:33.296
One, so that you can contribute more

00:12:33.296 --> 00:12:35.589
and two, so that hopefully
we can not just understand

00:12:35.589 --> 00:12:37.879
other people more, but
maybe appreciate them more

00:12:37.879 --> 00:12:39.249
and create the kinds of connections

00:12:39.249 --> 00:12:40.691
that can stop some of the challenges

00:12:40.691 --> 00:12:42.288
that we face in our society today.

00:12:42.288 --> 00:12:44.015
They're only going to get magnified

00:12:44.015 --> 00:12:46.210
by the very technology
that's connecting us.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.226
'Cause it's making us intersect

00:12:48.226 --> 00:12:50.568
and that intersection
doesn't always create

00:12:50.568 --> 00:12:52.486
the view of everybody
now understands everybody

00:12:52.486 --> 00:12:54.364
and everybody appreciates everybody.

00:12:54.364 --> 00:12:57.613
So, I've had an obsession
basically for 30 years.

00:12:57.613 --> 00:12:59.841
And that obsession has been what makes

00:12:59.841 --> 00:13:01.983
the difference in the
quality of people's lives?

00:13:01.983 --> 00:13:03.467
What makes a difference
in their performance

00:13:03.467 --> 00:13:04.430
'cause that's what I got hired to do.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.661
I got to produce a result now.

00:13:05.661 --> 00:13:07.142
That's what I've done for 30 years.

00:13:07.142 --> 00:13:09.286
I get the phone call when the athlete

00:13:09.286 --> 00:13:10.912
is burning down on national television

00:13:10.912 --> 00:13:13.251
and they were ahead by five strokes

00:13:13.251 --> 00:13:15.323
and now they can't get back on the course.

00:13:15.323 --> 00:13:16.167
And I got to do something right now

00:13:16.167 --> 00:13:17.833
to get the result or nothing matters.

00:13:17.833 --> 00:13:19.761
I get the phone call when
the child is going to

00:13:19.761 --> 00:13:22.301
commit suicide and I got
to do something right now.

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:24.538
And in 29 years, I'm
very grateful to tell ya,

00:13:24.538 --> 00:13:26.091
I've never lost one in 29 years.

00:13:26.091 --> 00:13:27.911
That doesn't mean I won't some day,

00:13:27.911 --> 00:13:28.744
but I haven't done it.

00:13:28.744 --> 00:13:29.577
And the reason is an understanding

00:13:29.577 --> 00:13:32.644
of these human needs that I
want to talk to you about.

00:13:32.644 --> 00:13:34.552
So, when I get those
calls about performance

00:13:34.552 --> 00:13:36.523
that's one thing, like
how to you make a change?

00:13:36.523 --> 00:13:39.133
But also I'm looking to see what is it

00:13:39.133 --> 00:13:41.979
that's shaping that person's
ability to contribute,

00:13:41.979 --> 00:13:44.052
to do something beyond themselves.

00:13:44.052 --> 00:13:45.920
So, maybe the real question is, you know,

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.217
I look at life and say
there's two master lessons.

00:13:48.217 --> 00:13:50.492
One is there's the science of achievement,

00:13:50.492 --> 00:13:51.549
which almost everyone in this room

00:13:51.549 --> 00:13:53.102
is mastered to in an amazing stent.

00:13:53.102 --> 00:13:54.219
That's how do you take the invisible

00:13:54.219 --> 00:13:55.247
and make it visible, right?

00:13:55.247 --> 00:13:56.262
How do you take what you're dreaming about

00:13:56.262 --> 00:13:57.095
and make it happen?
(snapping fingers)

00:13:57.095 --> 00:13:58.945
Whether it be your
business, your contribution

00:13:58.945 --> 00:14:00.744
to society, money, whatever it is for you.

00:14:00.744 --> 00:14:02.217
Your body, your family.

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:04.758
But the other lesson of
life that is rarely mastered

00:14:04.758 --> 00:14:06.455
is the art of fulfillment.

00:14:06.455 --> 00:14:07.742
'Cause science is easy, right?

00:14:07.742 --> 00:14:09.226
We know the rules, you write the code,

00:14:09.226 --> 00:14:11.036
you follow the, and you get the result.

00:14:11.036 --> 00:14:12.172
Once you know the game, you just,

00:14:12.172 --> 00:14:14.205
you know, you up the anti, don't you?

00:14:14.205 --> 00:14:16.675
But when it comes to
fulfillment, that's an art.

00:14:16.675 --> 00:14:18.370
And the reason is it's about appreciation

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.028
and it's about contribution.

00:14:20.028 --> 00:14:22.068
You can only fill so much by yourself.

00:14:22.068 --> 00:14:23.976
So, I've had an interesting laboratory

00:14:23.976 --> 00:14:25.838
to try to answer the
question of the real question

00:14:25.838 --> 00:14:27.330
which is what's the
difference in somebody's life

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:29.382
if you look at somebody like those people

00:14:29.382 --> 00:14:30.906
that you've given everything to.

00:14:30.906 --> 00:14:33.060
Like, all the resources
they say they need.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.441
You gave them not a
hundred dollar computer,

00:14:34.441 --> 00:14:35.478
you gave them the best computer.

00:14:35.478 --> 00:14:36.830
You gave them love, you gave them joy.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.363
You were there to comfort them.

00:14:38.363 --> 00:14:39.561
And those people very often,

00:14:39.561 --> 00:14:41.042
and you know some of them I'm sure

00:14:41.042 --> 00:14:42.304
and that the rest of their life with all

00:14:42.304 --> 00:14:44.408
this love, education, money and background

00:14:44.408 --> 00:14:47.158
spending their life going
in and out of rehab.

00:14:47.158 --> 00:14:48.045
And then you meet people that

00:14:48.045 --> 00:14:50.060
have been through ultimate pain.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:53.347
Psychologically, sexually,
spiritually, emotionally abused

00:14:53.347 --> 00:14:55.136
and not always, but often they become

00:14:55.136 --> 00:14:58.131
some of the people that
contribute the most to society.

00:14:58.131 --> 00:15:00.854
So, the question we got
to ask ourselves really is

00:15:00.854 --> 00:15:03.201
what is it, what is it that shapes us?

00:15:03.201 --> 00:15:04.877
And we live in a therapy culture.

00:15:04.877 --> 00:15:05.742
Most of us don't do that,

00:15:05.742 --> 00:15:07.070
but the culture's a therapy culture.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:10.433
And what I mean by that is the
mindset that we are our past.

00:15:10.433 --> 00:15:11.553
And everybody in this room, you wouldn't

00:15:11.553 --> 00:15:12.984
be in this room if you bought that theory,

00:15:12.984 --> 00:15:16.293
but the most of society
thinks biography is destiny.

00:15:16.293 --> 00:15:17.982
The past equals the future.

00:15:17.982 --> 00:15:19.566
And of course it does if you live there,

00:15:19.566 --> 00:15:20.858
but what people in this room know

00:15:20.858 --> 00:15:22.492
and what we have to
remind ourselves though,

00:15:22.492 --> 00:15:24.158
'cause you can know
something intellectually.

00:15:24.158 --> 00:15:26.994
You can know what to do and
then not use it, not apply it.

00:15:26.994 --> 00:15:28.303
So, really what we got to remind ourselves

00:15:28.303 --> 00:15:30.692
is decision is the ultimate power.

00:15:30.692 --> 00:15:31.606
That's what it really is.

00:15:31.606 --> 00:15:33.699
Now, when you ask people, you know,

00:15:33.699 --> 00:15:34.845
have you failed to achieve something.

00:15:34.845 --> 00:15:35.995
How many have every failed to achieve

00:15:35.995 --> 00:15:37.588
something significant in your life, say I.

00:15:37.588 --> 00:15:38.866
(audience saying "I")

00:15:38.866 --> 00:15:40.688
Thanks for the interaction
on a high level there.

00:15:40.688 --> 00:15:42.098
(laughing)

00:15:42.098 --> 00:15:45.065
But if you ask people why
didn't you achieve something,

00:15:45.065 --> 00:15:46.621
somebody who's working for you, you know,

00:15:46.621 --> 00:15:48.336
or a partner or even yourself.

00:15:48.336 --> 00:15:49.402
When you fail to achieve a goal

00:15:49.402 --> 00:15:51.680
what's the reason people
say they fail to achieve?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.632
What do they tell ya?

00:15:52.632 --> 00:15:54.269
Don't have the, didn't know enough.

00:15:54.269 --> 00:15:55.727
Didn't have the knowledge, didn't have the

00:15:55.727 --> 00:15:56.718
(audience shouting out)
money.

00:15:56.718 --> 00:15:57.986
Didn't have the
(audience shouting out)

00:15:57.986 --> 00:15:59.887
time.
Didn't have the

00:15:59.887 --> 00:16:00.972
(audience shouting out)
technology.

00:16:00.972 --> 00:16:03.225
You know, I didn't have the right manager.

00:16:03.225 --> 00:16:04.058
(audience shouting out)

00:16:04.058 --> 00:16:05.332
Didn't have the Supreme Court.

00:16:05.332 --> 00:16:06.925
(laughing)

00:16:06.925 --> 00:16:09.342
(applauding)

00:16:26.075 --> 00:16:27.028
And what do all those, including

00:16:27.028 --> 00:16:28.543
the Supreme Court have in common?

00:16:28.543 --> 00:16:30.697
(laughing)

00:16:30.697 --> 00:16:34.170
They are a claim to you missing resources

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:35.460
and they may be accurate.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.313
You may not have the money.

00:16:36.313 --> 00:16:37.936
You may not have the Supreme Court,

00:16:37.936 --> 00:16:39.860
but that is not the defining factor.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:42.571
(laughing)

00:16:42.571 --> 00:16:44.988
(applauding)

00:16:46.248 --> 00:16:48.849
And you correct me if I'm wrong,

00:16:48.849 --> 00:16:50.820
the defining factor is never resources,

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.168
it's resourcefulness and
what I mean specifically,

00:16:53.168 --> 00:16:54.387
rather than just some phrase,

00:16:54.387 --> 00:16:58.113
is if you have emotion, human emotion,

00:16:58.113 --> 00:17:00.762
something that I experience from you

00:17:00.762 --> 00:17:01.990
day before yesterday that is at a level

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.756
that is as profound as
I've ever experienced,

00:17:03.756 --> 00:17:05.151
then if you'd communicated
with that emotion

00:17:05.151 --> 00:17:08.045
I believe you would have
beat his ass and won.

00:17:08.045 --> 00:17:10.462
(applauding)

00:17:12.149 --> 00:17:16.122
But how easy for me to
tell him what he should do.

00:17:16.122 --> 00:17:18.276
(laughing)

00:17:18.276 --> 00:17:19.443
Idiot Robbins.

00:17:20.469 --> 00:17:24.290
But I know when we watched the debates,

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.241
when we watched the debate at that time,

00:17:26.241 --> 00:17:28.218
there were emotions that
blocked people's ability

00:17:28.218 --> 00:17:30.162
to get this man's intellect and capacity

00:17:30.162 --> 00:17:32.324
and the way it came across
to some people in that day.

00:17:32.324 --> 00:17:34.075
'Cause I know people that wanted to vote

00:17:34.075 --> 00:17:37.959
in your direction and
didn't and I was upset.

00:17:37.959 --> 00:17:39.323
But there was emotion that was there.

00:17:39.323 --> 00:17:40.156
How many know what I'm talking about here?

00:17:40.156 --> 00:17:42.281
Say I.
(audience saying "I")

00:17:42.281 --> 00:17:45.339
So, emotion is it and if
we get the right emotion

00:17:45.339 --> 00:17:46.621
we can get ourselves to do anything.

00:17:46.621 --> 00:17:47.454
We can get through it.

00:17:47.454 --> 00:17:49.292
If you're creative enough,
playful enough, fun enough

00:17:49.292 --> 00:17:50.877
can you get through to anybody, yes or no?

00:17:50.877 --> 00:17:51.722
(audience saying "yes")

00:17:51.722 --> 00:17:52.575
If you don't have the money,

00:17:52.575 --> 00:17:54.871
but you're creative and determined
enough you find the way.

00:17:54.871 --> 00:17:56.293
So, this is the ultimate resource,

00:17:56.293 --> 00:17:58.983
but this is not the story
that people tell us, right?

00:17:58.983 --> 00:18:01.210
The story people tell us is
a bunch of different stories.

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:02.499
They tell us we don't have the resources,

00:18:02.499 --> 00:18:04.571
but ultimately, if you take a look here,

00:18:04.571 --> 00:18:06.156
flip it up if you would,

00:18:06.156 --> 00:18:07.578
they say what are all the
reasons they have in common,

00:18:07.578 --> 00:18:09.439
we've said that, next one please.

00:18:09.439 --> 00:18:11.479
He's broken my pattern,
that son of a bitch.

00:18:11.479 --> 00:18:13.729
(laughing)

00:18:14.983 --> 00:18:16.924
But I appreciated the
energy, I'll tell ya that.

00:18:16.924 --> 00:18:18.358
(laughing)

00:18:18.358 --> 00:18:19.943
What determines your resources?

00:18:19.943 --> 00:18:23.171
We've said decisions shape
destiny, which is my focus here.

00:18:23.171 --> 00:18:24.687
If decisions shape destiny,

00:18:24.687 --> 00:18:26.069
what determines it is three decisions.

00:18:26.069 --> 00:18:27.409
What are you going to focus on?

00:18:27.409 --> 00:18:29.654
Right now, you have to decide
what you're going to focus on.

00:18:29.654 --> 00:18:31.413
In this second, consciously
or unconsciously.

00:18:31.413 --> 00:18:32.356
The minute you decide to focus

00:18:32.356 --> 00:18:34.331
on something you got to give it a meaning.

00:18:34.331 --> 00:18:36.376
And whatever that meaning
is produces emotion.

00:18:36.376 --> 00:18:38.325
Is this the end or the beginning?

00:18:38.325 --> 00:18:39.993
Is God punishing me or rewarding me

00:18:39.993 --> 00:18:42.204
or is this the role of the dice?

00:18:42.204 --> 00:18:45.499
And emotion then creates what
we're going to do, or the action.

00:18:45.499 --> 00:18:46.840
So, think about your own life,

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:49.115
the decisions that have
shaped your destiny.

00:18:49.115 --> 00:18:50.334
And that sounds really heavy,

00:18:50.334 --> 00:18:52.346
but in the last five
or 10 years, 15 years,

00:18:52.346 --> 00:18:53.736
how about some decisions have you made,

00:18:53.736 --> 00:18:55.363
that if you made a different decision

00:18:55.363 --> 00:18:57.577
your life would be completely different?

00:18:57.577 --> 00:18:58.803
How many can think of one, honestly.

00:18:58.803 --> 00:19:00.053
Better or worse, say I.

00:19:00.053 --> 00:19:00.886
(audience saying "I")

00:19:00.886 --> 00:19:03.269
So, the bottom line is maybe
it was where to go to work

00:19:03.269 --> 00:19:04.671
and you met the love of your life there.

00:19:04.671 --> 00:19:05.786
Maybe it was a career decision.

00:19:05.786 --> 00:19:07.698
I know the Google geniuses I saw here,

00:19:07.698 --> 00:19:09.436
I mean, I understand that their decision

00:19:09.436 --> 00:19:11.840
was to sell their technology at first.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.114
What if they made that decision versus

00:19:13.114 --> 00:19:14.495
to build their own culture?

00:19:14.495 --> 00:19:15.407
How would the world be different?

00:19:15.407 --> 00:19:17.684
How would their lives be
different, their impact?

00:19:17.684 --> 00:19:20.131
The history of our world
is these decisions.

00:19:20.131 --> 00:19:21.431
When a woman stands up and says

00:19:21.431 --> 00:19:24.490
"no I won't go to the back of the bus"

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:25.629
she didn't just affect her life.

00:19:25.629 --> 00:19:27.811
That decision shaped our culture.

00:19:27.811 --> 00:19:29.761
Or someone standing in front of a tank.

00:19:29.761 --> 00:19:31.773
Or being in a position
like Lance Armstrong

00:19:31.773 --> 00:19:34.575
and someone says to you,
you got testicular cancer.

00:19:34.575 --> 00:19:35.663
That's pretty tough for any male,

00:19:35.663 --> 00:19:39.323
especially if you ride a bike.
(laughing)

00:19:39.323 --> 00:19:41.424
You got it in your brain,
you got it in your lungs,

00:19:41.424 --> 00:19:43.976
but what was his decision
on what to focus on?

00:19:43.976 --> 00:19:45.732
Different than most
people, what did it mean?

00:19:45.732 --> 00:19:46.726
It wasn't the end, it was the beginning.

00:19:46.726 --> 00:19:47.743
What am I going to do?

00:19:47.743 --> 00:19:49.511
He goes off and wins seven championships

00:19:49.511 --> 00:19:51.217
he never once won before the cancer

00:19:51.217 --> 00:19:55.055
because he got emotional
fitness, psychological strength.

00:19:55.055 --> 00:19:56.573
That's the difference in human beings

00:19:56.573 --> 00:19:58.693
that I've seen of the three
million that I've been around.

00:19:58.693 --> 00:20:01.063
'Cause that's about my lab,
I've had three million people

00:20:01.063 --> 00:20:02.555
from 80 different countries that I've had

00:20:02.555 --> 00:20:04.952
the chance to interact with
over the last 29 years.

00:20:04.952 --> 00:20:07.462
And after awhile, patterns become obvious.

00:20:07.462 --> 00:20:09.799
You see that South America and Africa

00:20:09.799 --> 00:20:11.535
may be connected in a certain way, right?

00:20:11.535 --> 00:20:14.095
Other people say "oh, that
sounds ridiculous", it's simple.

00:20:14.095 --> 00:20:16.504
So what shapes Lance, what shapes you

00:20:16.504 --> 00:20:18.685
two invisible forces, very quickly.

00:20:18.685 --> 00:20:19.602
One, state.

00:20:20.953 --> 00:20:22.660
We all have had times, have you had

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.542
a time that you did something

00:20:23.542 --> 00:20:24.680
and after you did it
you thought to yourself

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:26.915
I can't believe I said that,
I can't believe I did that.

00:20:26.915 --> 00:20:28.227
That was so stupid, who's been there?

00:20:28.227 --> 00:20:29.638
Say I.
(audience saying "I")

00:20:29.638 --> 00:20:30.733
Have you ever done something
and after you do it you go

00:20:30.733 --> 00:20:32.930
(clearing throat)
That was me.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.442
(laughing)

00:20:34.442 --> 00:20:37.013
Right, it wasn't your
ability, it was your state.

00:20:37.013 --> 00:20:39.938
Your model of the world is
what shapes you long term.

00:20:39.938 --> 00:20:42.174
Your model of the world is the filter.

00:20:42.174 --> 00:20:43.665
That's what's shaping us.

00:20:43.665 --> 00:20:44.876
That's what makes people make decisions.

00:20:44.876 --> 00:20:46.368
We want to influence
somebody, we got to know

00:20:46.368 --> 00:20:48.211
what already influences them.

00:20:48.211 --> 00:20:50.030
And it's made of of
three parts, I believe.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:52.478
First, what's your
target, what are ya after?

00:20:52.478 --> 00:20:54.469
Which I believe, it's not your desires.

00:20:54.469 --> 00:20:55.525
You can get your desires to goals.

00:20:55.525 --> 00:20:57.539
How many ever got a goal
into desire and though

00:20:57.539 --> 00:20:58.889
is this all there is,
how many have been there?

00:20:58.889 --> 00:21:00.370
Say I.
(audience saying "I")

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:01.835
So, it's needs we have.

00:21:01.835 --> 00:21:03.228
I believe there's six human needs.

00:21:03.228 --> 00:21:06.183
Second, once you know what the
target that's driving you is

00:21:06.183 --> 00:21:07.819
and that you uncover it for the truth.

00:21:07.819 --> 00:21:09.657
You don't form it, you uncover it.

00:21:09.657 --> 00:21:10.684
Then you find out what's your map.

00:21:10.684 --> 00:21:11.953
What's the belief systems that are telling

00:21:11.953 --> 00:21:13.631
ya how to get those needs.

00:21:13.631 --> 00:21:14.632
Some people think the
ways to get those needs

00:21:14.632 --> 00:21:15.610
is to destroy the world,

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:17.195
some people it's to build something,

00:21:17.195 --> 00:21:18.893
create something, love someone.

00:21:18.893 --> 00:21:20.466
And then there's the fuel you pick.

00:21:20.466 --> 00:21:22.814
So, very quickly, six needs,
let me tell ya what they are.

00:21:22.814 --> 00:21:24.509
First one, certainty.

00:21:24.509 --> 00:21:26.541
Now these are not goals or
desires, these are universal.

00:21:26.541 --> 00:21:27.812
Everyone needs certainty that they

00:21:27.812 --> 00:21:29.833
can avoid pain and at
least be comfortable.

00:21:29.833 --> 00:21:30.764
Now, how do you get it?

00:21:30.764 --> 00:21:32.384
Control everybody, develop a skill,

00:21:32.384 --> 00:21:34.993
give up, smoke a cigarette?

00:21:34.993 --> 00:21:36.923
If you got total certainty ironically,

00:21:36.923 --> 00:21:38.073
even though we all need that,

00:21:38.073 --> 00:21:39.576
like, if you're not
certain about your health

00:21:39.576 --> 00:21:41.675
or your children or money,
you don't think about much.

00:21:41.675 --> 00:21:43.732
If you're not sure the
ceilings going to hold up,

00:21:43.732 --> 00:21:45.491
you're not going to listen to any speaker.

00:21:45.491 --> 00:21:47.352
But while we go for certainty differently,

00:21:47.352 --> 00:21:49.831
if we get total certainty, we get what?

00:21:49.831 --> 00:21:50.664
What do you feel if you're certain?

00:21:50.664 --> 00:21:51.497
You know, what's going to happen,

00:21:51.497 --> 00:21:52.330
when it's going to happen,
how it's going to happen,

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:53.163
what would you feel?

00:21:53.163 --> 00:21:54.571
(audience shouting out)
Bored out of your mind,

00:21:54.571 --> 00:21:57.580
so God in her infinite wisdom
(laughing)

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.538
gave us a second human
need which is uncertainty.

00:22:00.538 --> 00:22:02.903
We need variety, we need surprise.

00:22:02.903 --> 00:22:04.233
How many of you here love surprises?

00:22:04.233 --> 00:22:05.604
Say I.
(audience saying "I")

00:22:05.604 --> 00:22:07.495
Bull shit, you like
the surprises you want.

00:22:07.495 --> 00:22:09.486
(laughing)

00:22:09.486 --> 00:22:11.184
The ones you don't want you call problems,

00:22:11.184 --> 00:22:14.037
but you need them, so
variety is important.

00:22:14.037 --> 00:22:15.573
Have you ever rented a video or a film

00:22:15.573 --> 00:22:18.234
that you've already seen, who's done this?

00:22:18.234 --> 00:22:19.361
Get a (blanked out) life.

00:22:19.361 --> 00:22:21.343
(audience laughing)

00:22:21.343 --> 00:22:22.541
Alright, while your doing it,

00:22:22.541 --> 00:22:24.389
you're certain it's good
because you've read it before,

00:22:24.389 --> 00:22:25.580
saw it before, but you're hoping

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:28.068
it's been long enough you've
forgotten it, that's variety.

00:22:28.068 --> 00:22:30.741
Third human need, critical, significance.

00:22:30.741 --> 00:22:33.483
We all need to feel
important, special, unique.

00:22:33.483 --> 00:22:34.723
You can get it by making more money.

00:22:34.723 --> 00:22:36.227
You can do it by being more spiritual.

00:22:36.227 --> 00:22:37.800
You can do it by getting yourself

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.588
in a situation where you put more tattoos

00:22:39.588 --> 00:22:42.342
and earrings in places
humans don't want to know.

00:22:42.342 --> 00:22:44.049
Whatever it takes, the fastest way

00:22:44.049 --> 00:22:46.049
to do this if you have no background,

00:22:46.049 --> 00:22:47.592
no culture, and no believe in resources

00:22:47.592 --> 00:22:49.543
or resourcefulness is violence.

00:22:49.543 --> 00:22:51.465
If I put a gun to your head
and I live in the hood,

00:22:51.465 --> 00:22:54.012
instantly I'm significant,
zero to ten, how high?

00:22:54.012 --> 00:22:54.905
Ten.

00:22:54.905 --> 00:22:56.666
How certain am I that you're
going to respond to me?

00:22:56.666 --> 00:22:58.048
Ten.

00:22:58.048 --> 00:22:59.165
How much uncertainty, who knows

00:22:59.165 --> 00:23:00.768
what's going to happen
next, kind of exciting.

00:23:00.768 --> 00:23:02.213
Like, climbing up into a cave

00:23:02.213 --> 00:23:03.612
and doing that stuff
all the way down there,

00:23:03.612 --> 00:23:04.944
total variety and uncertainty

00:23:04.944 --> 00:23:06.958
and it's significant, isn't it?

00:23:06.958 --> 00:23:09.019
So you're willing to
risk your life for it.

00:23:09.019 --> 00:23:10.287
So, that's why violence
has always been around

00:23:10.287 --> 00:23:12.676
and will be around unless
we a conscientious change

00:23:12.676 --> 00:23:13.977
as a species.

00:23:13.977 --> 00:23:15.286
Now, you can get
significance a million ways,

00:23:15.286 --> 00:23:17.508
but to be significant you got
to be unique and different.

00:23:17.508 --> 00:23:19.166
Here's what we really need,

00:23:19.166 --> 00:23:21.117
connection and love, fourth need.

00:23:21.117 --> 00:23:23.116
We all want it, most people
settle for connection

00:23:23.116 --> 00:23:25.574
'cause love's to scary,
don't want to get hurt.

00:23:25.574 --> 00:23:27.537
Who here has ever been hurt
in an intimate relationship?

00:23:27.537 --> 00:23:29.283
Say I.
(audience saying "I")

00:23:29.283 --> 00:23:30.300
If you don't raise your hand you lie

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:31.498
about other shit too, come on.

00:23:31.498 --> 00:23:32.625
(audience laughing)

00:23:32.625 --> 00:23:33.629
And you're going to get hurt again.

00:23:33.629 --> 00:23:35.176
Aren't you glad you came
to this positive visit?

00:23:35.176 --> 00:23:36.262
(audience laughing)

00:23:36.262 --> 00:23:38.240
But here's what's true, we need it.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:40.581
We can do it through
intimacy, through friendship,

00:23:40.581 --> 00:23:43.080
through prayer, through walking in nature.

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:44.569
If nothing else works for you, get a dog.

00:23:44.569 --> 00:23:45.599
Don't get a cat, get a dog

00:23:45.599 --> 00:23:46.574
'cause if you leave for two minutes

00:23:46.574 --> 00:23:47.822
it's like you've been gone for six months

00:23:47.822 --> 00:23:49.285
when you show back up again
five minutes later, right?

00:23:49.285 --> 00:23:50.678
(audience laughing)

00:23:50.678 --> 00:23:51.693
Now, these first four needs,

00:23:51.693 --> 00:23:53.462
every human finds a way to meet.

00:23:53.462 --> 00:23:54.812
Even if ya lie to yourself, even if ya

00:23:54.812 --> 00:23:56.416
have split personalities.

00:23:56.416 --> 00:23:59.058
But the last two needs,
the first four needs

00:23:59.058 --> 00:24:00.634
are called the needs of the personality,

00:24:00.634 --> 00:24:01.679
it's what I call it.

00:24:01.679 --> 00:24:04.318
The last two are the needs of the spirit.

00:24:04.318 --> 00:24:05.600
And this is where fulfillment comes.

00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:06.961
You won't get fulfillment
from the first four.

00:24:06.961 --> 00:24:08.233
You'll figure a way, smoke, drink,

00:24:08.233 --> 00:24:09.980
do whatever, meet the first four,

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:12.723
but the last two, number
five, you must grow.

00:24:12.723 --> 00:24:15.572
We all know the answer here,
if you don't grow you what?

00:24:15.572 --> 00:24:16.493
If a relationship is not growing,

00:24:16.493 --> 00:24:18.240
if a business is not growing,
if you're not growing.

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.277
It doesn't matter how much money you have,

00:24:19.277 --> 00:24:21.500
how many friends you have,
how many people love you,

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:22.789
you feel like hell.

00:24:22.789 --> 00:24:24.751
And the reason we grow, I believe,

00:24:24.751 --> 00:24:27.036
is so we have something to give of value.

00:24:27.036 --> 00:24:29.932
'Cause the sixth needs is to
contribute beyond ourselves.

00:24:29.932 --> 00:24:32.074
'Cause we all know, corny as it sounds,

00:24:32.074 --> 00:24:33.864
the secret to living is giving.

00:24:33.864 --> 00:24:35.904
We all know life's not
about me, it's about we.

00:24:35.904 --> 00:24:37.786
This culture knows that,
this room knows that

00:24:37.786 --> 00:24:38.709
and it's exciting.

00:24:38.709 --> 00:24:40.070
When you see Nicholas us here talking

00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:41.410
about his hundred dollar computer,

00:24:41.410 --> 00:24:42.540
the most passionate, exciting thing

00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:45.971
is here's a genius, but
he's got a calling now.

00:24:45.971 --> 00:24:48.737
You can feel the difference
in him and it's beautiful.

00:24:48.737 --> 00:24:50.473
And that calling can touch other people.

00:24:50.473 --> 00:24:52.028
In my own life, my life was touched

00:24:52.028 --> 00:24:54.263
because when I was 11
years old, Thanksgiving,

00:24:54.263 --> 00:24:56.762
no money, no food and
we're not going to starve,

00:24:56.762 --> 00:24:58.518
but my father was totally messed up.

00:24:58.518 --> 00:25:00.753
My mom was letting him
know how bad he messed up

00:25:00.753 --> 00:25:03.670
and somebody came to the
door and delivered food.

00:25:03.670 --> 00:25:05.011
My father made three decisions.

00:25:05.011 --> 00:25:06.239
I know what they were, briefly.

00:25:06.239 --> 00:25:08.474
His focus was this is charity.

00:25:08.474 --> 00:25:10.009
What does it mean, I'm worthless,

00:25:10.009 --> 00:25:12.732
What do I got to do, leave
my family, which he did.

00:25:12.732 --> 00:25:15.199
The time, one of the most
painful experiences of life.

00:25:15.199 --> 00:25:17.791
My three decisions gave
me a different path.

00:25:17.791 --> 00:25:20.694
I said focus on there's
food, what a concept.

00:25:20.694 --> 00:25:22.403
(laughing)

00:25:22.403 --> 00:25:23.732
Second, but this is what changed my life,

00:25:23.732 --> 00:25:25.471
this is what shaped me as a human being,

00:25:25.471 --> 00:25:27.583
somebody's gift, I don't
even know who it is.

00:25:27.583 --> 00:25:30.936
I thought, my father always
said no one give a (blanked out)

00:25:30.936 --> 00:25:32.521
and all of a sudden somebody I don't know,

00:25:32.521 --> 00:25:34.297
they're not asking for it,
just giving our family food,

00:25:34.297 --> 00:25:35.467
looking out for us.

00:25:35.467 --> 00:25:37.406
It made me believe
this, what does it mean?

00:25:37.406 --> 00:25:39.834
That strangers care.

00:25:39.834 --> 00:25:41.388
And what that made me decide
is that if strangers care

00:25:41.388 --> 00:25:42.964
about me and my family, I care about them.

00:25:42.964 --> 00:25:43.960
What am I going to do?

00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:45.605
I'm going to do something
to make a difference.

00:25:45.605 --> 00:25:48.042
So, when I was 17 I went
out one day on Thanksgiving,

00:25:48.042 --> 00:25:49.393
it was my target for years,

00:25:49.393 --> 00:25:50.815
have enough money, feed two families.

00:25:50.815 --> 00:25:51.985
It was the most fun thing
I ever did in my life,

00:25:51.985 --> 00:25:54.533
most moving, then next year I did four.

00:25:54.533 --> 00:25:55.682
I didn't tell anybody what I was doing.

00:25:55.682 --> 00:25:58.101
Next year eight, I wasn't
doing it for brownie points,

00:25:58.101 --> 00:25:59.520
but after eight I thought (blanked out),

00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:01.523
I could use dome help.
(audience laughing)

00:26:01.523 --> 00:26:03.392
So sure enough, I went
out and what did I do?

00:26:03.392 --> 00:26:05.211
I got my friends involved
and then I grew companies

00:26:05.211 --> 00:26:07.191
and then I got 11 companies
and I built a foundation

00:26:07.191 --> 00:26:09.282
and now 18 years later
I'm proud to tell ya

00:26:09.282 --> 00:26:11.051
that last year we fed two million people

00:26:11.051 --> 00:26:12.871
in 35 countries through our foundation,

00:26:12.871 --> 00:26:15.106
all during the holidays,
Thanksgiving, Christmas,

00:26:15.106 --> 00:26:16.079
in all the different
countries around the world.

00:26:16.079 --> 00:26:17.910
(audience applauding)
It's been fantastic.

00:26:17.910 --> 00:26:18.743
Thank you.

00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:21.303
So, I don't tell ya that to brag.

00:26:21.303 --> 00:26:23.651
I tell ya because I'm
proud of human beings

00:26:23.651 --> 00:26:25.793
because they get excited
to contribute once they've

00:26:25.793 --> 00:26:28.861
had the change to experience
it, not talk about it.

00:26:28.861 --> 00:26:30.893
So, finally, and I'm about out of time,

00:26:30.893 --> 00:26:33.768
the target that shapes you,

00:26:33.768 --> 00:26:34.956
here's what's different about people.

00:26:34.956 --> 00:26:36.704
We have the same needs, but are you

00:26:36.704 --> 00:26:38.735
a certainty freak, is
that what you value most?

00:26:38.735 --> 00:26:40.564
Or uncertainty?

00:26:40.564 --> 00:26:41.956
This man here couldn't
be a certainty freak

00:26:41.956 --> 00:26:43.765
if he climbed through those caves.

00:26:43.765 --> 00:26:45.533
Are you driven by significance or love?

00:26:45.533 --> 00:26:48.195
We all need all six, but
whatever your lead system is

00:26:48.195 --> 00:26:49.739
tilts you in a different direction.

00:26:49.739 --> 00:26:50.612
And as you move in a direction,

00:26:50.612 --> 00:26:52.467
you have a destination or destiny.

00:26:52.467 --> 00:26:54.319
The second piece is the map.

00:26:54.319 --> 00:26:55.782
Think of that as the operating system

00:26:55.782 --> 00:26:56.830
that tells ya how to get there

00:26:56.830 --> 00:26:59.236
and some people's map is
I'm going to save lives

00:26:59.236 --> 00:27:01.450
even if I die for other
people and there are firemen.

00:27:01.450 --> 00:27:03.867
Somebody else says I'm going
to kill people to do it.

00:27:03.867 --> 00:27:06.408
They're trying to meet the
same needs of significance.

00:27:06.408 --> 00:27:09.232
Right, they want to honor
God or honor their family,

00:27:09.232 --> 00:27:10.463
but they have a different map.

00:27:10.463 --> 00:27:11.566
And there are seven different beliefs,

00:27:11.566 --> 00:27:13.226
I can't go through them because I'm done.

00:27:13.226 --> 00:27:15.522
The last piece is emotion.

00:27:15.522 --> 00:27:17.783
I say one of the parts
of the map is like time.

00:27:17.783 --> 00:27:20.061
Some people's idea of a long
time is a hundred years.

00:27:20.061 --> 00:27:22.174
Somebody else says it's three
seconds, which is what I have.

00:27:22.174 --> 00:27:23.657
(audience laughing)

00:27:23.657 --> 00:27:25.515
And the last one I've already
mentioned that felt you.

00:27:25.515 --> 00:27:27.538
If you've got a target, you got a map.

00:27:27.538 --> 00:27:30.615
And let's say, I can't use
Google 'cause I love macs

00:27:30.615 --> 00:27:31.956
and they haven't made
it good for macs yet.

00:27:31.956 --> 00:27:33.509
So, if you use Mapquest,
how many have made

00:27:33.509 --> 00:27:35.045
this fatal mistake of
using Mapquest at sometime?

00:27:35.045 --> 00:27:36.679
(audience laughing)

00:27:36.679 --> 00:27:37.990
You use this thing and
you don't get there.

00:27:37.990 --> 00:27:39.584
Well, imagine if your beliefs guarantee

00:27:39.584 --> 00:27:41.128
you can never get to where you want to go.

00:27:41.128 --> 00:27:42.916
(audience laughing)

00:27:42.916 --> 00:27:45.061
And last thing is emotion.

00:27:45.061 --> 00:27:46.634
Now, here's what I'll
tell you about emotion.

00:27:46.634 --> 00:27:49.592
There are 6,000 emotions
that we all have words for

00:27:49.592 --> 00:27:50.881
in the english language, which is just

00:27:50.881 --> 00:27:52.477
a linguistic representation, right?

00:27:52.477 --> 00:27:53.654
It changes my language.

00:27:53.654 --> 00:27:57.394
But if your dominate
emotions, if I had more time,

00:27:57.394 --> 00:27:59.324
I have 20,000 people, or a thousand

00:27:59.324 --> 00:28:00.685
and I have them write
down all the emotions

00:28:00.685 --> 00:28:02.939
that they experience in an average week

00:28:02.939 --> 00:28:03.924
and I give them as long as they need.

00:28:03.924 --> 00:28:05.448
And on one side they're
writing empowering emotions,

00:28:05.448 --> 00:28:06.281
the others disempowering.

00:28:06.281 --> 00:28:07.746
Guess how many emotions people experience?

00:28:07.746 --> 00:28:09.221
Less than 12.

00:28:09.221 --> 00:28:11.709
And half of those make them
feel like (blanked out).

00:28:11.709 --> 00:28:14.878
So they got five or six good
freakin' feelings, right?

00:28:14.878 --> 00:28:16.260
It's like they feel happy, happy excited.

00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:17.540
Oh, (blanked out) frustrated, frustrated,

00:28:17.540 --> 00:28:18.860
overwhelmed, depressed.

00:28:18.860 --> 00:28:20.161
How many of you know somebody

00:28:20.161 --> 00:28:22.386
who no matter what happens
finds a way to get pissed off?

00:28:22.386 --> 00:28:23.290
How many knows somebody like this?

00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:24.581
(audience laughing)

00:28:24.581 --> 00:28:26.683
Or no matter what happens,
no matter what happens,

00:28:26.683 --> 00:28:28.706
they find a way to be happy or excited.

00:28:28.706 --> 00:28:30.737
How many know somebody like this, come on?

00:28:30.737 --> 00:28:32.615
When nine one one happened,
and I'll finish with this,

00:28:32.615 --> 00:28:33.988
I was in Hawaii.

00:28:33.988 --> 00:28:36.537
I was with 2,000 people from 45 countries.

00:28:36.537 --> 00:28:38.771
We were translating four
languages simultaneously

00:28:38.771 --> 00:28:41.079
for a program that I was
conducting for a week.

00:28:41.079 --> 00:28:43.688
The night before was
called emotional mastery.

00:28:43.688 --> 00:28:46.065
I got up, had no plan for this, and I said

00:28:46.065 --> 00:28:48.462
we had all these fireworks,
I do crazy (blanked out),

00:28:48.462 --> 00:28:50.242
fun stuff and then at the end I stopped.

00:28:50.242 --> 00:28:51.184
I had this plan I was going to say,

00:28:51.184 --> 00:28:53.046
but I never do what I'm going
to say and all of a sudden

00:28:53.046 --> 00:28:55.830
I said "when do people
really start to live,

00:28:55.830 --> 00:28:57.841
when they face death".

00:28:57.841 --> 00:28:58.816
And I went through this whole thing about

00:28:58.816 --> 00:29:00.381
if you weren't going
to get off this island,

00:29:00.381 --> 00:29:03.071
if nine days from now
you were going to die,

00:29:03.071 --> 00:29:06.049
who would you call, what would
you say, what would you do?

00:29:06.049 --> 00:29:09.361
One woman, well, that night
was when 9-1-1 happened.

00:29:09.361 --> 00:29:10.824
One woman had come to the seminar

00:29:10.824 --> 00:29:13.181
and when she came there,
her previous boyfriend

00:29:13.181 --> 00:29:15.009
had been kidnapped and murdered.

00:29:15.009 --> 00:29:16.988
Her friend, or her new boyfriend,

00:29:16.988 --> 00:29:18.289
wanted to marry her and she said no.

00:29:18.289 --> 00:29:19.824
He said if you leave and
go to that Hawaii thing,

00:29:19.824 --> 00:29:21.174
it's over with us, she said it's over.

00:29:21.174 --> 00:29:22.607
When I finished that night, she called him

00:29:22.607 --> 00:29:23.827
and left a message, true story,

00:29:23.827 --> 00:29:26.751
at the top of the World
Trade Center where he worked,

00:29:26.751 --> 00:29:29.078
saying "honey, I love you,
I just want you to know

00:29:29.078 --> 00:29:31.676
I want to marry you, it was stupid of me".

00:29:31.676 --> 00:29:34.432
She was asleep 'cause
it was three a.m. for us

00:29:34.432 --> 00:29:35.923
when he called her back from the top

00:29:35.923 --> 00:29:37.956
and said "honey, I can't
tell you what this means".

00:29:37.956 --> 00:29:39.956
He said "I don't know
how to tell you this,

00:29:39.956 --> 00:29:43.392
but you gave me the greatest
gift 'cause I'm going to die".

00:29:43.392 --> 00:29:45.352
And she played the recording
for us in the room,

00:29:45.352 --> 00:29:46.765
she was on Larry King later.

00:29:46.765 --> 00:29:49.488
And he said "you're probably
wondering how on earth

00:29:49.488 --> 00:29:50.400
this could happen to you twice".

00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:52.485
And he said "all I can say to you is this

00:29:52.485 --> 00:29:54.395
must be God's message to
you, honey, for now on

00:29:54.395 --> 00:29:56.622
every day, give your all, love your all,

00:29:56.622 --> 00:29:58.845
don't let anything every stop you".

00:29:58.845 --> 00:30:00.816
She finishes and a man stands up

00:30:00.816 --> 00:30:03.185
and he says "I'm from
Pakistan, I'm a muslim,

00:30:03.185 --> 00:30:05.359
I'd love to hold your
hand and say I'm sorry,

00:30:05.359 --> 00:30:08.292
but frankly this is retribution".

00:30:08.292 --> 00:30:10.743
I can't tell you the rest
'cause I'm out of time.

00:30:10.743 --> 00:30:13.743
(audience shouting)

00:30:15.842 --> 00:30:17.592
Really, are you sure?

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:22.127
(audience applauding)

00:30:23.023 --> 00:30:24.023
Ten seconds.

00:30:27.493 --> 00:30:29.545
Ten seconds and I want to
be respectful, ten seconds.

00:30:29.545 --> 00:30:31.324
All I can tell ya is that
I brought this man on stage

00:30:31.324 --> 00:30:33.324
with a man from New York who worked in

00:30:33.324 --> 00:30:34.331
the World Trade Center 'cause I had

00:30:34.331 --> 00:30:35.854
about 200 New Yorkers there.

00:30:35.854 --> 00:30:37.359
More than 50 lost their entire companies,

00:30:37.359 --> 00:30:39.765
their friends, marking
off their palm pilots.

00:30:39.765 --> 00:30:43.454
One financial trader, this
woman, made a steel balling,

00:30:43.454 --> 00:30:45.729
30 friends crossing off that all died.

00:30:45.729 --> 00:30:47.030
And what I did to people is said

00:30:47.030 --> 00:30:49.720
what are we going to focus on?

00:30:49.720 --> 00:30:52.301
What does this mean and
what are we going to do?

00:30:52.301 --> 00:30:54.019
And I took the group and
got people to focus on

00:30:54.019 --> 00:30:55.563
if you didn't lose somebody today,

00:30:55.563 --> 00:30:57.867
you're focus is going to be
how to serve somebody else.

00:30:57.867 --> 00:30:58.801
There were people, one woman got up

00:30:58.801 --> 00:31:00.805
and she was so angry and
screaming and yelling.

00:31:00.805 --> 00:31:01.992
Then I found out she wasn't from New York.

00:31:01.992 --> 00:31:04.836
She's not an American, she
doesn't know anybody here.

00:31:04.836 --> 00:31:06.711
I said "do you always get
angry", she said "yes".

00:31:06.711 --> 00:31:09.042
Guilty people got guilty,
sad people got sad.

00:31:09.042 --> 00:31:10.374
And I took these two men and did

00:31:10.374 --> 00:31:12.487
what I call an indirect negotiation.

00:31:12.487 --> 00:31:14.425
Jewish man with family in
the occupied territories,

00:31:14.425 --> 00:31:15.970
some New Yorker who would have died

00:31:15.970 --> 00:31:17.606
if he was at work that day

00:31:17.606 --> 00:31:19.151
and this man who wanted to be a terrorist

00:31:19.151 --> 00:31:20.318
and made it very clear.

00:31:20.318 --> 00:31:21.996
And the integration that
happened is on a film,

00:31:21.996 --> 00:31:23.363
which I'll be happy to send you.

00:31:23.363 --> 00:31:24.514
So, you can really see
what actually happened

00:31:24.514 --> 00:31:26.068
instead of my verbalization of it.

00:31:26.068 --> 00:31:27.694
But the two of them not only came together

00:31:27.694 --> 00:31:29.238
and changed their beliefs
and models of the world,

00:31:29.238 --> 00:31:30.690
but they worked together to bring,

00:31:30.690 --> 00:31:33.110
for almost four years
now, to various mosques

00:31:33.110 --> 00:31:35.209
and synagogues the idea
of how to create peace.

00:31:35.209 --> 00:31:36.674
And he wrote a book which is called

00:31:36.674 --> 00:31:39.083
"My Jihad, My Way Of Peace".

00:31:39.083 --> 00:31:40.363
So, transformation can happen.

00:31:40.363 --> 00:31:43.155
So, my invitation to you is this,

00:31:43.155 --> 00:31:45.988
explore your web, the web in here.

00:31:46.822 --> 00:31:49.208
The needs, the beliefs, the emotions

00:31:49.208 --> 00:31:51.091
that are controlling you, for two reasons.

00:31:51.091 --> 00:31:53.720
So there's more of you
to give and achieve too.

00:31:53.720 --> 00:31:55.438
We all want to do it, but I mean give.

00:31:55.438 --> 00:31:56.678
'Cause that's what's going to fill you up.

00:31:56.678 --> 00:32:00.030
And, secondly, so you can
appreciate, not just understand,

00:32:00.030 --> 00:32:01.229
that's intellectual, that's the mind,

00:32:01.229 --> 00:32:03.604
but appreciate what's
driving other people.

00:32:03.604 --> 00:32:04.834
It's the only way our
world is going to change.

00:32:04.834 --> 00:32:06.308
God bless you, thank you,
I hope this was served.

00:32:06.308 --> 00:32:10.475
- Tony Robbins
(audience applauding)

00:32:12.148 --> 00:32:13.499
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:32:13.499 --> 00:32:16.629
I hope you enjoyed, this is
a test new series for us.

00:32:16.629 --> 00:32:18.043
I'm curious what you think about it.

00:32:18.043 --> 00:32:20.794
Should the Did You Know series continue?

00:32:20.794 --> 00:32:22.806
Is there someone you'd like us to profile

00:32:22.806 --> 00:32:24.268
in the next Did You Know series?

00:32:24.268 --> 00:32:26.292
Let us know, did you hate this series

00:32:26.292 --> 00:32:27.816
and never want to see it again.

00:32:27.816 --> 00:32:29.338
Leave it in the comments below.

00:32:29.338 --> 00:32:31.351
We're going to use your
feedback to make some decisions.

00:32:31.351 --> 00:32:33.412
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Jennifer Clarke.

00:32:33.412 --> 00:32:35.087
Jennifer, thank you so
much for picking a copy up

00:32:35.087 --> 00:32:37.365
of my book Your One
Word it really, really,

00:32:37.365 --> 00:32:38.865
really, really means a lot to me.

00:32:38.865 --> 00:32:40.350
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:32:40.350 --> 00:32:41.591
I believe in you.

00:32:41.591 --> 00:32:43.519
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:32:43.519 --> 00:32:45.634
and whatever your one word is.

00:32:45.634 --> 00:32:48.294
Much love and I'll see ya soon.

00:32:48.294 --> 00:32:50.581
